@startuml mrta_mode_button_architecture

title MRTA mode button — where each piece lives across the three repos

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam DefaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #888888
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C060

legend right
  Companion diagrams:
  - class design: sim_dotbot_mrta_ws_target_class_diagram.puml
  - server state machine: mrta_mode_button_state_machine.puml
  Contract + open items: Button.md
end legend

' Declared top -> bottom so the request/data flow reads straight down.

package "PyDotBot  (external repo — controller + web console)" as PD {
  package "console-web/  (unified web UI)" as WEB {
    [MRTA pill\nMrtaToggle.tsx · useMrta.ts (poll 1.5s) · mrta.ts · api.ts] as PILL
    [map · drive pad · waypoints UI\n(a click is PUT .../waypoints)] as MAPUI
  }
  [dotbot/server.py — /mrta/{path} reverse-proxy -> mrta_url\n(default http://localhost:8002, prefix stripped)] as PROXY
  [controller — REST /controller/*  +  WS /controller/ws/status] as CTRL
}
note right of PILL
  Polls GET /mrta/status every 1.5s. Nothing behind the
  proxy -> greyed "MRTA N/A", the resting state.
end note
note right of PROXY
  The whole PyDotBot backend delta: ~40 lines, modelled on
  the /swarmit/* proxy. Threads one URL (mrta_url /
  --mrta-url / DOTBOT_MRTA_URL). The controller knows one
  URL, nothing else about MRTA.
end note

package "dotbot-logistics  (this repo — the bridge)" as BRIDGE {
  [mrta_server.py — thin CLI (argparse -> serve())] as SERVERCLI
  [mrta_mode/server.py — MrtaMode\nstate machine + session lifecycle · FastAPI · session on a thread] as SERVER
  package "mrta_mode/  (drives core + pibt)" as MM {
    [MRTASession\nconnect / start / stop / tick / handle_click / halt_all] as SESSION
    [ControllerStatusListener · LivePositionStore · ManualClickTranslator\nWaypointCommandClient · GridStateManager] as COLLAB
  }
}
note right of SERVER
  MrtaMode builds a fresh MRTASession on every ON (fleet
  snapshotted at connect()), and runs tick() on a worker
  thread — never on the loop serving the routes.
end note
note right of MM
  Restartability + OFF path:
  - listener.stop() stops the WS thread and joins it
  - wait_until_all_arrived() is interruptible (no OFF stall)
  - an empty waypoint list == "Stop nav" -> cancel the target
  - halt_all() / WaypointCommandClient.send_stop() is the OFF path,
    run stop-flag -> wake arrival-wait -> join tick thread -> PUT [] per address
end note

package "mapf-simulation  (external repo, pip-installed)" as MAPF {
  [core: WorldEngine · Grid2D · Agent · Coordinates2D] as CORE
  [pibt: PIBTPlanner · LifelongGoalOrchestrator] as PIBT
}

PILL   -down->  PROXY   : GET /mrta/status\nPOST /mrta/mode {on}
PROXY  -down->  SERVER  : GET /status\nPOST /mode {on}
note on link
  body {state, bots, detail};  state = off | connecting | on | stopping.
  'unavailable' is inferred client-side from 404/502/timeout — never sent.
end note
SERVERCLI -down-> SERVER : python mrta_server.py
SERVER -down->  SESSION : one MRTASession per ON
SESSION -right-> COLLAB
SESSION -down->  CORE   : advance_time_step()
SESSION -down->  PIBT   : set_target(agent_id, cell)
COLLAB -left->   CTRL   : GET /controller/dotbots\nPUT .../0/waypoints\nWS /controller/ws/status
CTRL   -up->     MAPUI  : operator drives bots from the same UI as always

@enduml
